    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-16",
    "scope": "Three actually inspected west/south exterior pictures and standard viewer PMTiles/DEM only.No bespoke datasets or redistributed reference images.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tampereen_Tuomiokirkko.jpg",
        "author": "MatteoTRphoto",
        "date": "2017-08-24",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected west front:rough varied grey/warm granite masonry,large circular leaded window beneath broad steep gable,small horizontal slot row,lower transverse red-tile canopy and projecting gabled portal. Unequal west towers have red tapering spires and green tips. Tall southwest tower has triple pointed louver apertures,slit below and a small round roofed stair turret near its foot. Main spire tip and lower approach are cropped;vegetation obscures some base. No glass artwork or fine stone sculpture copied."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tampereen_tuomiokirkko_2.JPG",
        "author": "M62",
        "date": "2007-08-04 (Exif2007-08-03)",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-2.5/3.0 or GFDL1.2+",
        "observed": "Actually inspected south oblique:long red-tile main roof,large transverse south stone gable with circular leaded light and lower pointed-window rhythm,additional pointed side light,small roofed buttress/stair projections. Tall southwest tower has triple pointed belfry panels,plain shaft and segmented tapered red spire with small corner roofs. Low rough-stone red-capped park enclosure and gabled pedestrian gate are visible;trees obscure northern/rear church and exact wall ends."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tampere_Cathedral_Apr2012_001.jpg",
        "author": "Methem (Mikko J. Putkonen)",
        "date": "2012-04",
        "license": "CC-BY-3.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected whole southwest tower to green finial,red spire with lower corner caps and a narrow mid-spire vent band,plain granite shaft,three pointed belfry louvers;long main roof and transverse south rose gable with lower arcade rhythm. Confirms tower/spire proportions and low red-capped gate wall. Rear/north roofs remain partly hidden by trees."
      }
    ]
